WEEK 1 – DAY 4: INTRODUCTION TO TRANSFORMERS

1. GPT
   GPT stands for Generative Pre-trained Transformer.

- Generative: Generates and predicts the next token.
- Pre-trained: Trained on large amounts of data.
- Transformer: The neural network architecture used by GPT.

2. Neural Networks

- Inspired loosely by the human brain.
- Consist of connected artificial neurons.
- Learn patterns from training data to make predictions.
- Deep learning uses multiple layers of connected neurons.

3. Transformer Architecture

- Introduced by Google researchers in 2017.
- Based on the research paper "Attention Is All You Need".
- Uses self-attention to identify important parts of an input sequence.
- Helps train larger models and process more data efficiently.

4. Evolution of GPT

- GPT-1: 2018
- GPT-2: 2019
- GPT-3: 2020
- ChatGPT (GPT-3.5): 2022
- GPT-4: 2023
- GPT- 4o : 2024

5. Self-Attention
   Helps a model identify which parts of an input sequence are important when processing information.

6. Transformer Alternatives

- State Space Models (SSMs)
- Hybrid Architectures

Transformers remain the predominant architecture for LLMs.

KEY TAKEAWAY
Transformers made it possible to train and scale large language models more efficiently, reducing training time and costs.
